nt": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QJPK5WL8TernwzCZNNTjH8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AvKRzmhHUMWKBMtF5UpHgW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy was unhealthy in production (~18% error rate across us-east, us-west, eu-west). It was rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, and the rollback is now live in all regions. Note: payments-api v5.1.0 also shows as degraded (18% error rate) and should be checked.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.88}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011vL4FAPZfCq1Tj7o148EUA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again: the error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n1. **Finding the service:** There's no service named plain \"payments.\" I found payments-api first and tried to roll it back from v5.1.0 to v5.0.0. The approver turned that down and said the problem was in payments-worker, so payments-api was not changed.\n2. **Rollback:** payments-worker was running v3.4.0, which was marked unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. v3.3.0 is now live in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n3. **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for payments-worker, and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0, which shows as degraded and had an 18% error rate when I checked it, before the rollback. I didn't check it again afterwards. It may just have been feeling the payments-worker failures, but someone should look at it to make sure it has recovered. I mentioned this in the incident summary.", "type": "text"}]}]}